[41.632776, "o", " left pip in a broken state — the `pip3` script existed and pointed to the right Python, but the actual `pip` module couldn't be imported because its code was missing.\r\n\r\n**Fix:** Removed the orphaned `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` directory and re-ran `python3 -m ensurepip --default-pip`, which extracted the bundled `pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl` back into site-packages. Pip is now fully functional (`pip 24.3.1`, Python 3.13).\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=implementor model=qwen3.6-35b tools=20 surface=de1fadd2f308\r\n"]
